e distribution of the 2019  settlement freeze represented the Glo  claimants and have vital knowledge and  expertise based on their involvement in  that case and this will allow us to work  at PACE on the design of a scheme of the  jfsa and Fritz to give those in the Glo  similar compensation to their non-glo  peers  as promised in March we will informally  consult with members of the Glo about  the proposed schemes operation and I'm  also pleased to announce that members of  the Glo group will be able to claim  reasonable legal fees as part of  participating in the compensation scheme  and I hope that will allay any concerns  that they may have about meeting the  costs of seeking legal advice and  support when applying to the scheme  turning now to progress on compensation  for overturned criminal convictions I'm  pleased to report to the house the  interim payments are progressing well as  of 29th of June there have been 75  overturned convictions with the most  recent convictions being Ableton just in  recent weeks and the post office has  received 74 applications for interim  payments including several new  applications recently  67 offers have been accepted by and paid  out to payments totally nearly seven  million pounds  this marks significant progress with 10  additional interim payments made to  postmasters since I updated the Bayes  select committee on the 11th of January  2022 and I'm pleased that these interim  payments have helped to deliver an early  down payment on the compensation due to  effective postmasters in advance of full  and final compensation packages being  agreed  now for those postmasters with an  overturned conviction who have already  submitted Quantified claims I can share  that we are working with post office to  agree part payment of agreed elements of  claims such as loss of earnings wherever  possible and will continue to do so with  additional claims when they're submitted  now taking this step should enable us to  avoid undue de